IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ira-dates`

-- Industrial Relations Act 1979 (WA) -- the rules the employee's questions share: the actors and steps, the one
-- regulative rule (a step to be taken within the days the Act allows), the state system, the s 7 definition of
-- employee, the s 29AA salary bar, serious contraventions and the maximum penalties, damaging action, and the s 23A
-- remedies.
--
-- Sourced from the Western Australian Legislation website at 2026-09-07: "Industrial Relations Act 1979", State of
-- Western Australia, licensed under CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). See SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Industrial Relations Act 1979 -- shared rules`

§§ `Actors and steps`

DECLARE `Actor` IS ONE OF
    `the employee`
    `the Commission`

DECLARE `Step` IS ONE OF
    `refer the unfair dismissal claim`
    `apply to the industrial magistrate's court`
    `start to deal with the application`

-- The Act's time limits as duties: the actor MUST take the step WITHIN the days allowed, LEST the time has passed.
-- WITHIN counts days from the day the period runs from (day 0), so a step on the last day is on time.
GIVEN `the actor` IS AN `Actor`, `the step` IS A `Step`, `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Actor` `Step`
`the step must be taken` `the actor` `the step` `within` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the actor`
    MUST EXACTLY `the step`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the actor` BECAUSE "the time limit fixed by the Industrial Relations Act 1979 has passed"

-- Runs the rule over one event (the step, on its day) or, where the step has not been taken, a wait until the day
-- asked about. On the stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH, so FULFILLED means on
-- time and anything else too late. It takes no DEONTIC input and is not exported.
GIVEN `the actor` IS AN `Actor`, `the step` IS A `Step`, `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
      `was it taken` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the trace of` `the actor` `the step` `within` `the days allowed` `taken` `was it taken` `at` `the day number` `is fulfilled` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`the step must be taken` `the actor` `the step` `within` `the days allowed`) 0 `the events`
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHERE
        `the events` MEANS
            IF `was it taken`
            THEN LIST (EVENT `the actor` `the step` `the day number`)
            ELSE LIST (WAITUNTIL `the day number`)

-- Whether a step taken on a day is within a time limit whose last day is given, counted from a starting day.
GIVEN `the actor` IS AN `Actor`, `the step` IS A `Step`, `the starting day` IS A DATE, `the last day` IS A DATE, `the day of the step` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the actor` `takes` `the step` `from` `the starting day` `by` `the last day` `on` `the day of the step` `in time` IF
    `the trace of` `the actor` `the step` `within` (`the days from` `the starting day` `to` `the last day`) `taken` TRUE `at` (`the days from` `the starting day` `to` `the day of the step`) `is fulfilled`

§§ `The state system (FW Act s 14 and s 80A)`

-- The Act's own definition of employer (s 7(1)) reaches every person employing an employee. Whether a state law can
-- govern the employment turns on the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth): a national system employer is covered by that Act, which
-- excludes state industrial law, unless the employer is one the FW Act s 14(2) lets the State declare and the
-- regulations under s 80A(2) declare it (Industrial Relations (General) Regulations 1997 r 7 and Schedule 4, from
-- 1 January 2023). Both facts are borrowed and asked.
GIVEN `national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN, `declared under section 80A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the state system reaches the employment` `national system employer` `declared under section 80A` MEANS
    IF (NOT `national system employer`) OR `declared under section 80A`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 7 -- employee`

-- s 7(1) employee "means" (a) an individual employed by an employer to do work for hire or reward, including as an
-- apprentice, or (b) an individual whose usual status is that of an employee. s 7A: whether the individual is employed
-- is decided by the real substance, practical reality and true nature of the relationship, a judgment asked as a fact.
GIVEN `employed in substance` IS A BOOLEAN, `for hire or reward` IS A BOOLEAN, `usual status of an employee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an employee under section 7` `employed in substance` `for hire or reward` `usual status of an employee` IF
        (`employed in substance` AND `for hire or reward`)
    OR  `usual status of an employee`

§§ `s 29AA -- the salary bar`

-- s 29AA(3), (4): the Commission must not determine the claim if (a) no industrial instrument (an award, a Commission
-- order not prescribed, an industrial agreement or an EEA, s 29AA(5)) applies to the employment and (b) the contract
-- provides for a salary exceeding the prescribed amount ($90 000 a year, indexed under regs 5(1) and 6; asked).
GIVEN `an industrial instrument applies` IS A BOOLEAN, `the salary` IS A NUMBER, `the prescribed amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the salary bar applies` `an industrial instrument applies` `the salary` `the prescribed amount` IF
        (NOT `an industrial instrument applies`)
    AND `the salary` GREATER THAN `the prescribed amount`

§§ `ss 83(4A), 83E(1), 83EA -- serious contraventions and the maximum penalties`

DECLARE `Kind of person` IS ONE OF
    `a body corporate`
    `an individual`

-- s 83EA(2), (4): serious if committed knowingly (for a body corporate, authorised expressly, tacitly or impliedly,
-- s 83EA(3)), or recklessly: aware of a substantial risk that it would occur and, on the circumstances known, the risk
-- was unjustifiable to take.
GIVEN `knowingly` IS A BOOLEAN, `aware of a substantial risk` IS A BOOLEAN, `unjustifiable to take the risk` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a serious contravention` `knowingly` `aware of a substantial risk` `unjustifiable to take the risk` IF
        `knowingly`
    OR  (`aware of a substantial risk` AND `unjustifiable to take the risk`)

-- ss 83(4A), 83E(1): the same four figures for an entitlement provision and a civil penalty provision.
GIVEN `the person` IS A `Kind of person`, `serious` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum pecuniary penalty for` `the person` `serious` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `a body corporate` THEN IF serious THEN 930000 ELSE 93000
    WHEN `an individual` THEN IF serious THEN 180000 ELSE 18000

§§ `s 97 -- damaging action`

-- s 97: (a) for an employee, (b) for a prospective employee.
DECLARE `Action taken against me` IS ONE OF
    `dismissing me`
    `altering my position to my disadvantage`
    `refusing to promote or transfer me`
    `otherwise injuring me in relation to my employment`
    `threatening to do any of those things`
    `refusing to employ me`
    `discriminating in the terms or conditions offered to me`
    `threatening to refuse to employ me or to discriminate`
    `none of these`

-- s 97 damaging action "means" the listed acts: a closed definition.
GIVEN `the action` IS AN `Action taken against me`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is damaging action` `the action` IF
    CONSIDER `the action`
    WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `s 23A -- unfair dismissal remedies`

-- s 23A(3), (4), (5)(a), (5)(b), (6) in that order.
DECLARE `Remedy` IS ONE OF
    `reinstatement to my former position`
    `re-employment in another suitable position`
    `an order maintaining the continuity of my employment`
    `payment of the remuneration I lost because of the dismissal`
    `compensation for loss or injury caused by the dismissal`
